  "id": "extrinsic-reinforcement",
  "term": "extrinsic reinforcement",
  "definition": "Extrinsic reinforcement is behaviour change that is encouraged by outside rewards or consequences rather than by a person’s own inherent interest or motivation. In this context, it is presented as a behaviourist way of influencing action and is contrasted with intrinsic motivation.",
